Analyze the following CPU-intensive numerical algorithm processing an array of 10,000,000 items:

public async Task ProcessHeavyMatrixAsync(double[] data) {
    var tasks = new List<Task>();
    for (int i = 0; i < data.Length; i++) {
        int index = i;
        tasks.Add(Task.Run(() => {
            data[index] = Math.Sin(data[index]) * Math.Cos(data[index]);
        }));
    }
    await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
}

MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS:
1. Explain the performance collapse caused by Heap Allocation Overhead of millions of 'Task' objects and ThreadPool context switching saturation when using 'Task.Run' in a fine-grained loop for CPU-bound tasks.
2. Refactor the method using 'Parallel.For' or 'Parallel.ForEach' (synchronous or partitioned) to distribute work efficiently across CPU cores with zero Task allocation overhead on the Heap.

